(NEXA MOBILE - BATTERY CARE AND CHARGING GUIDE) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
14 TL
T*
() Tj
T*
/F1 12 Tf
(3. Battery Specifications and Fast Charging Profiles) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
14 TL
T*
(All models feature a 5000mAh high-density lithium-ion battery with smart cell protection.) Tj
T*
(Charging inputs: Nexa Lite up to 18W, Nexa One up to 33W 0 to 50 percent in 28 minutes,) Tj
T*
(and Nexa One Pro up to 67W Turbo Charge 0 to 100 percent in 42 minutes.) Tj
T*
(Charging Curve: Charging speed automatically tapers above 80 percent to safeguard battery chemistry.) Tj
T*
(Slow Charging Troubleshooting:) Tj
T*
(1. Verify that the cable is firmly connected to both the device and the wall adapter.) Tj
T*
(2. Inspect the USB-C port for pocket lint or debris using a dry, soft non-conductive brush.) Tj
T*
(3. Test with an alternate certified USB Type-C cable and a USB-PD compliant power source.) Tj
T*
(4. Avoid charging in direct sunlight or environments above 35 degrees Celsius.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
/F1 12 Tf
(4. Critical Safety Warnings - Battery Hazard Protocol) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
14 TL
T*
(If a device exhibits a swollen back cover, excessive heat, smoke, popping sounds, or chemical odor:) Tj
T*
(- Disconnect the charger immediately if it is safe to do so.) Tj
T*
(- Stop using the device and move it onto a non-flammable surface tile, concrete, or stone.) Tj
T*
(- Keep away from beds, sofas, curtains, and children.) Tj
T*
(- Do not attempt to puncture, press, or pry open the battery compartment.) Tj
T*
(- Contact Nexa Mobile Safety Support immediately for emergency hazardous exchange.) Tj
T*
() Tj
ET
endstream
>>
