(NEXA MOBILE - HARDWARE AND DISPLAY DIAGNOSTICS) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
14 TL
T*
() Tj
T*
/F1 12 Tf
(5. Display Settings and Touchscreen Calibration) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
14 TL
T*
(Nexa One Pro supports dynamic refresh rates from 60Hz up to 120Hz for fluid scrolling.) Tj
T*
(To enable 120Hz: Navigate to Settings > Display > Screen Refresh Rate > Dynamic 120Hz.) Tj
T*
(If experiencing touch unresponsiveness or frozen screens:) Tj
T*
(- Perform a hardware force reboot: Press and hold Power + Volume Down together for 10 seconds.) Tj
T*
(- If display shows colored vertical lines or black blotches, this indicates physical panel trauma.) Tj
T*
(- Remove thick non-certified tempered glass screen protectors that may impair touch sensitivity.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
/F1 12 Tf
(6. 50MP Camera Optimization and Lens Care) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
14 TL
T*
(The primary 50MP Sony sensor utilizes Optical Image Stabilization OIS to eliminate motion blur.) Tj
T*
(Best practices for clear photos:) Tj
T*
(- Clean the camera lens glass using a lint-free microfiber cloth.) Tj
T*
(- If the camera app crashes, go to Settings > Apps > Camera > Storage > Clear Cache.) Tj
T*
(- Close other active applications that may be accessing the camera hardware in the background.) Tj
T*
(- Ensure imaging firmware is up to date under Settings > System > System Update.) Tj
T*
() Tj
ET
endstream
>>
